\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Where Cross the crowded ways of life,
\par Where sound the cries of race and clan,
\par Above the noise of selfish strife,
\par We hear Thy voice, O Son of Man.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. In haunts of wretchedness and need,
\par On shadowed thresholds dark with fears,
\par From paths where hide the lures of greed,
\par We catch the vision of Thy tears.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. From tender childhood's helplessness,
\par From woman's grief, man's burden toil,
\par From femished souls, from sorrow's stress,
\par Thy heart has never known recoil.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. The cup of water given for Thee
\par Still holds the freshness of Thy grace;
\par Yet long these multitudes to see
\par The sweet compassion of Thy face.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O Master, from the mountain side,
\par Make haste to heal these hearts of pain;
\par Among these restless throngs abide,
\par O tread the city's streets again:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Till sons of men shall learn Thy love,
\par And follow where Thy feet have trod;
\par Till glorious from Thy heaven above,
\par Shall come the City of our God.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

